       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Confirming it doesn't fix either problem:\n\n- **The dose is still dangerous.** 50 mg of amlodipine is five times the maximum daily dose, and no one should give it to this patient. A prescriber's sign-off wouldn't change that either. Any clinician would be expected to question an order like this.\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** As you said, you're not a clinician, so your confirmation can't stand in for one. This rule protects the patient and also protects you and the hospital from liability.\n\n**If the patient needs blood pressure treatment:** Please contact the attending physician or the on-call prescriber for the medicine service. If they order a standard dose (2.5\u201310 mg once daily), I'll enter it as soon as they authorize it.\n\n**If this was a test of the system's safety checks:** The order was not entered."
